We are requesting a formal commercial quotation and technical intake confirmation for a batch of nine (9) diverse material specimens requiring accredited density and specific gravity determination under ISO/IEC 17025 standards (ASTM D792 / ASTM B311 / ASTM D1622 equivalents).

All specimens are part of pre-registration protocol ARM2-BENCH-PROTOCOL-v1.0. Below is the complete schedule of materials, required test methodologies, and specialized handling instructions.

SCHEDULE OF TEST SPECIMENS & METHODOLOGIES
1. Aluminum 6061-T6511 - extruded bar stock (cut piece) - ASTM D792 / ASTM B311 (Archimedes immersion). Standard metal densitometry.
2. Borosilicate Glass 3.3 (COE 33) - solid rod (homogeneous, clear) - ASTM D792 (Archimedes immersion). Verify solid rod (no internal voids or tubing).
3. Stainless Steel 304/304L - cold-finish round bar - ASTM D792 / ASTM B311 (Archimedes immersion). Standard metal densitometry.
4. Binder-Free CVD Diamond - optical-window grade single-crystal / polycrystalline plate - Archimedes immersion or high-precision pycnometry. Critical: must be binder-free (no cobalt/metal catalyst phase).
5. Virgin PTFE - extruded solid rod - ASTM D792 Method A. Standard polymer immersion.
6. Lithium Metal (99.9% 3N) - 1.0 g in sealed glass ampoule - non-aqueous immersion or helium pycnometry. Hazmat / water-reactive: ampoule must be opened under inert atmosphere (argon/nitrogen glovebox) by lab personnel. Water immersion is strictly prohibited.
7. Rigid Polyurethane Foam (PBLT-20) - high-density urethane (HDU) tooling board - ASTM D1622 / ISO 845 (bulk density). Critical: must measure bulk/apparent density including closed cells. Do not run skeletal gas pycnometry alone.
8. XPS Foam Board (FOAMULAR NGX) - extruded polystyrene panel section - ASTM D1622 (bulk density). Measure apparent/bulk density.
9. Osmium Metal (99.95%) - ~1.0 g arc-melted bead / bar - high-precision immersion / micro-pycnometry. High density (~22.59 g/cm3); requires micro-balance precision (target 0.06% uncertainty class).

TECHNICAL & ADMINISTRATIVE REQUIREMENTS
* Accreditation: all testing under Element Houston's A2LA ISO/IEC 17025 scope (Cert. 1480.05). Please confirm ASTM D792 / B311 / D1622 (or equivalent applicable methods) are formally covered under your current local accreditation schedule.
* Replicate protocol: each specimen run in triplicate (three independent determinations per specimen).
* Lithium consignment: prior to shipment, please confirm receiving protocols for a 1.0 g sealed glass ampoule of water-reactive lithium metal (UN 1415, Class 4.3) and capacity for inert-atmosphere ampoule breaching.
* Deliverables: Certified Test Reports including raw mass values, immersion fluid densities/temperatures, calculated specific gravities, and estimated measurement uncertainty budgets for each specimen.

